  title={Semi-Supervised and Disentangled Causal Discovery for Analyzing Fault Propagation in Microservices}, 
  year={2026},
  volume={14},
  number={},
  pages={30613-30626},
  abstract={While troubleshooting fault propagation in a microservice-based system is labor-intensive for operators, it is critical to their decision-making process for maintaining availability and reliability. Efficient troubleshooting can significantly accelerate fault recovery and help strengthen preventive measures. Therefore, fault analysis techniques demand high interpretability of not only the fault location but also the fault propagation. However, existing works have mainly focused on developing root cause analysis, which cannot capture such structures among microservices. In this paper, we propose semi-supervised causal structure learning to capture the fault propagation across microservices from the time series data supported by continuous structure learning. We also introduce disentanglement learning to enhance the generalizability of out-of-distribution graphs of new faults. Extensive experiments on microservice-based system datasets demonstrate that the semi-supervised approach is effective, and the proposed model is superior to baseline methods.},
